    gameId: 'asso-pigliatutto-scopa',
    icon: '🃏',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: "1. **Play**: Player plays one card. 2. **Capture**: If the card matches the rank of a table card, it captures it. If it matches the sum of multiple table cards, it captures them. 3. **The Ace Rule**: If you play an Ace, you take ALL cards on the table (unless there is an Ace on the table, in which case you must capture only the Ace). 4. **Scopa**: Clearing the table earns 1 point (a 'Scopa'). Exception: Playing an Ace to clear the table usually does NOT award a Scopa point unless the Ace captured a single Ace. 5. **Refill**: When hands are empty, dealer deals 3 more. 6. **End**: Last player to take a trick collects any remaining table cards.",
    Player: "1. **Play**: Player plays one card. 2. **Capture**: If the card matches the rank of a table card, it captures it. If it matches the sum of multiple table cards, it captures them. 3. **The Ace Rule**: If you play an Ace, you take ALL cards on the table (unless there is an Ace on the table, in which case you must capture only the Ace). 4. **Scopa**: Clearing the table earns 1 point (a 'Scopa'). Exception: Playing an Ace to clear the table usually does NOT award a Scopa point unless the Ace captured a single Ace. 5. **Refill**: When hands are empty, dealer deals 3 more. 6. **End**: Last player to take a trick collects any remaining table cards.",
    objective: "Score 11 points (or 21) by capturing cards, specifically Coins, Sevens, and the 'Primiera'.",
    gameplay: "1. **Play**: Player plays one card. 2. **Capture**: If the card matches the rank of a table card, it captures it. If it matches the sum of multiple table cards, it captures them. 3. **The Ace Rule**: If you play an Ace, you take ALL cards on the table (unless there is an Ace on the table, in which case you must capture only the Ace). 4. **Scopa**: Clearing the table earns 1 point (a 'Scopa'). Exception: Playing an Ace to clear the table usually does NOT award a Scopa point unless the Ace captured a single Ace. 5. **Refill**: When hands are empty, dealer deals 3 more. 6. **End**: Last player to take a trick collects any remaining table cards.",
    keyRules: [
      'Must Capture: If you can capture, you must. You cannot simply discard if a capture is possible (though you can choose WHICH capture if there are multiple).',
      'Ace Priority: If an Ace is on the table, playing an Ace only captures that Ace (standard capture rule). If NO Ace is on the table, playing an Ace captures EVERYTHING.',
      'Scopa Point: Awarded for clearing the table, marked by turning a card face-up in the trick pile. (Note: Ace-sweeps typically yield 0 points).',
      'Scoring Categories: Settebello (7 of Coins), Denari (Most Coins), Carte (Most Cards), Primiera (Best 4-card set).',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: '2 players (heads-up) or 4 players (two partnerships).',
      deck: '40-card Italian deck (Coins, Cups, Swords, Batons). If using a standard 52-card deck, remove 8s, 9s, and 10s. Kings=10, Queens=9, Jacks=8.',
      equipment: 'Standard Italian deck, score sheet.',
      dealing: 'Dealer gives 3 cards to each player and places 4 cards face-up on the table. When players run out of cards, 3 more are dealt until the deck is empty.',
    },
    turnFlow: "1. **Play**: Player plays one card. 2. **Capture**: If the card matches the rank of a table card, it captures it. If it matches the sum of multiple table cards, it captures them. 3. **The Ace Rule**: If you play an Ace, you take ALL cards on the table (unless there is an Ace on the table, in which case you must capture only the Ace). 4. **Scopa**: Clearing the table earns 1 point (a 'Scopa'). Exception: Playing an Ace to clear the table usually does NOT award a Scopa point unless the Ace captured a single Ace. 5. **Refill**: When hands are empty, dealer deals 3 more. 6. **End**: Last player to take a trick collects any remaining table cards.",
