      "Turn-flow example: 1. **Play**: Player plays one card. 2. **Capture**: If the card matches the rank of a table card, it captures it. If it matches the sum of multiple table cards, it captures them. 3. **The Ace Rule**: If you play an Ace, you take ALL cards on the table (unless there is an Ace on the table, in which case you must capture only the Ace). 4. **Scopa**: Clearing the table earns 1 point (a 'Scopa'). Exception: Playing an Ace to clear the table usually does NOT award a Scopa point unless the Ace captured a single Ace. 5. **Refill**: When hands are empty, dealer deals 3 more. 6. **End**: Last player to take a trick collects any remaining table cards.",
